4.1.0b18 20001126
	Fixed memory leak in cleanup.c: HC->incoming wasn't free(2)ed.
5.0.0b20001216
	The daemon will no longer bind to any socket for accepting
	new sessions, but will expect to be started by spawnd and
	accept messages on stdin. No more forking. Plain and easy :-))
5.0.0b20001222
	Removed all IPC dependencies. Removed classes and share-based
	load balancing. Merged RFC1413 querying code to make identifier
	obsolete. Worked like a charm, and the loss of functionality
	by dropping the user class concept seems minor in comparision
	to the semaphore troubles on Solaris. I like the new concept.
2001010500
	Fixed identd query bug.
2001032300
	Switched to MAVIS scheme.
2001032700
	Now compiles with -D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64, which seems sufficient
	to enable 64bit file i/o support for Linux. Chances are that the
	source changes cover Solaris, too.
2001040100
	Finally using mmap() for reading data from disk. Improves transfer
	performance by about 10%. Your milleage may vary. This is sort of
	experimental and may need more testing.
2001040200
	Use sendfile(), if available.
2001040700
	mmap() and I/O buffering revised. Attempt to keep I/O buffers filled.
2001041600
	Once again, mmap() et al. revised. Now mapping larger mmap()
	regions. ASCII mode conversion re-done. chunk.c introduced.
	Dynamic fallback sendfile->mmap->read
2001061600
	Found & fixed a bug in offset assignment in chunk.c which caused
	corrupted ASCII transfers.
2001102000
	Found & fixed another offset related bug in chunk.c
2001102800
	Found & fixed one more offset related bug in chunk.c
2001122400
	Various internal changes. Conversion to io_* routines completed.
	STOU no longer uses mktemp(3).
2002010500
	Conversion to new mavis API completed.
2002011100
	Don't process whole mmap(2)ed file area, but at most bufsize bytes.
	Fixed iomode initialization for conversions if sendfile supported.
